course: dictionary
lesson: 14963
title: Relocate: moving to a new place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «When the Patel family got a new job in Leeds, they had to relocate.» The clues are a new job and a new town. To relocate means to move to a new place to live or work, so the family moved house.
explain: You can also relocate something or someone. «The rangers relocated the injured owl to a safe place in the woods.» The owl was moved to a new place. The rangers did the moving.
explain: Relocate is a more formal word than move, so you will often meet it in letters, news reports and at work. Try swapping in move: if the sentence still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Relocate means to move to a new place to live or work.
fact: To relocate something or someone means to move them to a new place.
fact: Relocate is a formal word, so «move» often fits in the same sentence.
fact: «Relocate to» is a common phrase, as in «They will relocate to the coast next year.»
fact: In science, animals are sometimes relocated to safer places to protect them.
exercise: «The family will relocate to Bristol after the summer.» What does relocate mean here? | To paint a house a new colour | To lose your way in a town | *To move to a new place to live | To visit a place for one day
exercise: «The rangers relocated the injured deer to a quiet forest.» What was moved? | The rangers | The sun | *The deer | The quiet forest
exercise: Which word could replace relocate in «The school will relocate to a bigger building»? | forget | sleep | freeze | *move
test: «My cousin had to relocate for work and now lives three hundred miles away.» Why did the cousin relocate? | To go on holiday | To learn to swim | To visit a friend for the weekend | *To take a new job in a new place
test: Which phrase means the same as relocate? | forget the way | cook a meal | *move house | sing loudly
exam: «The council will relocate the bus stop because the road is being mended.» What does relocate mean here? | To throw the bus stop away | To mend the road itself | To close the road for ever | *To move the bus stop to a new place
